mailbox: cix: add audited ACPI support and harden transfers

CIX Sky1 firmware describes mailbox controllers as CIXHA001 devices and
uses a numeric cix,mbox_dir property.  Retain the existing device-tree
string property as a fallback, without assuming the property encoding
from the firmware-node type.

Native firmware describes the AP-to-PM SCMI shared-memory prefix inside
the mailbox resource.  If that unshifted ACPI resource is already busy,
probe the independently requestable register window at +0x80; upgraded
tables that already describe the shifted window continue down the normal
path.

Return transfer-helper failures instead of reporting invalid payloads as
success, keep the mailbox interrupt available for suspend-time SCMI
traffic on kernel lines that predate that upstream fix, and register a
module exit path.  Correct the message-size documentation to match the
7-bit field used by both Linux and the CIX TF-A firmware ABI.

This consolidates CIX vendor ordinal 0001 with the overlay's former
30180 shared-memory-overlap fix and the mailbox half of 30170.  The
driver's OF-or-ACPI applicability is now established at its introduction
instead of relying on a late Kconfig repair.

